.TH K2HVECPMTOOL "1" "September 2026" "K2HVECPMTOOL" "Vector database/search Library"
.SH NAME
K2HVECPMTOOL \- A standalone tool for generating projection matrix data used by K2HVEC.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B k2hvecpmtool
[OPTIONS] [ \--help(-h) ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
A dedicated tool for generating, updating, and loading the Projection Matrix used internally during data storage and similarity search processing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\--help(-h)\fR
Displays usage instructions and the list of available options.
.TP
\fB\--bit_size(-bs)\fR <number>
Specifies the bit count (size) within the range of 16 to 512 (default: 48).
.TP
\fB\--dimension_size(-ds)\fR <number>
Specifies the number of vector dimensions within the range of 512 to 8192 (default: 4096).
.TP
\fB\--name(-n)\fR <string>
Specifies the array name for the Projection Matrix (default: "pm").
.TP
\fB\--version(-v)\fR <string>
Specifies the array version for the Projection Matrix (default: "1.0").
.TP
\fB\--output(-o)\fR <file path>
Specifies the destination file path (outputs to stdout if this option is omitted).
.TP
\fB\--debug(-d)\fR
Prints detailed debug log messages.
.TP
\fB\--sourcecode(-s)\fR
Specifies the output format for source code generation (intended for internal developer use only).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBVECDBGMODE\fR
VECDBGMODE environment sets debugging message level. The value is set as SILENT, ERR, WAN, INFO or DUMP.
When SIGUSER1 signal is caught, the debugging message level is bumpup. The level is changed as order by SILENT, ERR, WAN, INFO, DUMP, SILENT...
.TP
\fBVECDBGFILE\fR
VECDBGFILE environment sets the file which is debugging message.
.SH SEE ALSO
.TP
